+@ Optional reusable adapter. The map owner may point the Station host here.
+@ Other gyms need their own approved trainer/adapter; listed names do not grant stamps.
+TaichungGym_EventScript_StationChallenge::
+	lock
+	faceplayer
+	setvar VAR_0x8004, TAICHUNG_GYM_OLD_STATION
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptIsComplete
+	goto_if_eq VAR_RESULT, TRUE, TaichungGym_StationAlreadyComplete
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_OFFER
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptGetStationMessage
+	msgbox gStringVar4, MSGBOX_YESNO
+	goto_if_eq VAR_RESULT, NO, TaichungGym_StationDeclined
+	setvar VAR_0x8004, TAICHUNG_GYM_OLD_STATION
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TRAINER_TAICHUNG_STATION_JUN
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptPrepareChallenge
+	goto_if_eq VAR_RESULT, FALSE, TaichungGym_StationUnavailable
+	goto_if_eq VAR_0x40FB, 2, TaichungGym_StationBattleChinese
+	trainerbattle_single TRAINER_TAICHUNG_STATION_JUN, TaichungGym_Text_StationIntroEn, TaichungGym_Text_StationDefeatEn, TaichungGym_StationAfterBattle
+	goto TaichungGym_StationBattleSkipped
+
+TaichungGym_StationBattleChinese::
+	trainerbattle_single TRAINER_TAICHUNG_STATION_JUN, TaichungGym_Text_StationIntroZh, TaichungGym_Text_StationDefeatZh, TaichungGym_StationAfterBattle
+	goto TaichungGym_StationBattleSkipped
+
+@ Native trainer flags can bypass a battle (for example, a quest-log replay).
+@ Cancel tracking and release controls rather than trusting an old battle result.
+TaichungGym_StationBattleSkipped::
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptCancelChallenge
+	goto TaichungGym_StationNotRecorded
+
+TaichungGym_StationAfterBattle::
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptGetResult
+	goto_if_ne VAR_RESULT, TAICHUNG_GYM_RESULT_WON, TaichungGym_StationNotRecorded
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_COMPLETE
+	goto TaichungGym_StationMessage
+
+TaichungGym_StationAlreadyComplete::
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_ALREADY_COMPLETE
+	goto TaichungGym_StationMessage
+
+TaichungGym_StationDeclined::
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_DECLINED
+	goto TaichungGym_StationMessage
+
+TaichungGym_StationUnavailable::
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_UNAVAILABLE
+	goto TaichungGym_StationMessage
+
+TaichungGym_StationNotRecorded::
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_NOT_RECORDED
+
+TaichungGym_StationMessage::
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptGetStationMessage
+	msgbox gStringVar4
+	release
+	end
diff --git a/docs/localization/taichung-city-localization.md b/docs/localization/taichung-city-localization.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..08a63ae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/localization/taichung-city-localization.md
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# Native city language coverage
+
+This follow-up starts from native integration `d72e04f6cb6184bc8116119fceaeceae1f280f3f`. The mapper's city text at commit `f099c12040a9f8678312e50eda8e8089515a45aa` is the source inventory. No district geometry, warps, spawn, startup scripts, exploration preferences or progression code is changed here.
+
+## Translation corpus
+
+`taichung-city-zh.additions.json` is an additive fragment, not a complete generator configuration. Its `translations` object supplies all 22 `TaichungCity_Text_*` symbols from `data/scripts/taichung_city.inc`: the Station and Greenway guides, ten exterior landmark signs, and ten hall hosts. It also replaces the old Greenway-specific Chinese `Taichung_Text_Welcome` with:
+
+> 歡迎來到臺中！
+> 從這裡展開城市冒險。
+
+The existing English welcome already says the city adventure starts here and remains appropriate at the Station spawn. All original English city strings remain the fallback. Translations preserve the current provisional hall status: city-league challenges are being prepared. They do not invent final leaders, rosters or completed gyms.
+
+The longest authored Chinese line is 14 glyphs, conservatively 168 pixels at the native 12-pixel advance. Paragraph controls and intentional line breaks are retained. Every mapped symbol is present in the city script, with no missing or unexpected city labels. The full temporary configuration produces 54 runtime pointer translations and 328 glyphs, including the existing native menus and City Pass.
+
+## Compact district names
+
+`src/taichung_city_names.c` supplies localized names for exactly the three new sections. `GetMapName` uses them only when Chinese is active; English and every other location use the original lookup and fill behavior. It does not change the mapper's generated region-map data.
+
+| Section | Existing English | Chinese | Encoded bytes with terminator |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `MAPSEC_TAICHUNG_OLD_CITY` | OLD TAICHUNG | 臺中舊城 | 17 |
+| `MAPSEC_TAICHUNG_GREENWAY` | TAICHUNG GREENWAY | 草悟道 | 13 |
+| `MAPSEC_TAICHUNG_XITUN` | TAICHUNG XITUN | 臺中西屯 | 17 |
+
+FireRed has a 19-byte region-map name buffer and a 25-byte popup buffer. Chinese glyphs occupy four encoded bytes each. These compact names fit both without allocating more RAM; compile-time checks enforce the 19-byte limit. Their displayed widths are 48, 36 and 48 pixels, within the normal 112-pixel title area. The fragment's `mapSectionNames` records this naming contract for review; only its `translations` object needs merging into the root corpus.
+
+The generated `TaichungIsChinese` now reads the current saved variable directly, with its existing null-pointer guard. It must not call `VarGet`, which can replay historical quest-log values back into the current save. This follows the parent-owned canonical generator update; global event-data semantics remain unchanged.
+
+## Reproduction and integration
+
+Main owns the root corpus and helpers. Merge the fragment's translations into the current root corpus, preserving its menus, additional characters and other workstreams. Regenerate the union after gameplay/preferences and localization are merged; do not replace the root corpus with this fragment.
+
+For an isolated build, first compose a temporary full configuration into an ignored artifact directory:
+
+```python
+import json
+from pathlib import Path
+
+base = json.loads(Path("/absolute/project/scripts/map-content/taichung-zh.json").read_text())
+fragment = json.loads(Path("docs/localization/taichung-city-zh.additions.json").read_text())
+base["translations"].update(fragment["translations"])
+Path("/absolute/ignored/city-translation-config.json").write_text(
+    json.dumps(base, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n"
+)
+```
+
+Then invoke the existing parent helpers with both explicit paths:
+
+```sh
+TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE=/absolute/game/worktree \
+TAICHUNG_TRANSLATION_CONFIG=/absolute/ignored/city-translation-config.json \
+python3 /absolute/project/scripts/generate-chinese-font.py
+
+TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE=/absolute/game/worktree \
+bash /absolute/project/scripts/build-game.sh
+```
+
+Generation requires Pillow. A second run is byte-identical. The startup script and bridge source hashes remain unchanged by regeneration, so the shared exploration-startup call can be merged independently.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+The native build succeeds. EWRAM uses 261,088 of 262,144 bytes, leaving 1,056 bytes; IWRAM uses 29,824 of 32,768. Added glyphs, translations and district names are constant ROM data and do not enlarge EWRAM. Native map-name symbol sizes are 17/13/17 bytes in the compiled object. `git diff --check` passes.
+
+The isolated emulator pass used the text build with SHA-1 `892567b0eee4e053288adb536ae8cf5e619aebdd`, before the subsequent raw-language-getter change. It visibly verified the generic Chinese welcome at the actual Station spawn, Chinese four-starter labels and a successful Bulbasaur selection, both pages of the Old Station sign including the hall explanation, and the Chinese district name `臺中舊城` fitting the native Save summary. The production browser locale bridge also adopted Chinese from this new ROM's metadata and shifted EWRAM address.
+
+The final raw-getter build preserves the same glyphs, text and layout and has SHA-1 `e0acbec0f7e27e64d703f466b0ee12097be30ab3`, SHA-256 `731c53a4ccedb5626fd7d696c875ce9ff60acc69466b0c5148cb77022b30f8a3`. No save was overwritten during this text check. The test tab was closed and its local server stopped. Evidence is under the parent project's ignored `artifacts/worktrees/8d9e3f9b98e8/` directory:
+
+- `qa-city-localization-welcome.jpg`
+- `qa-city-localization-station-sign.jpg`
+- `qa-city-localization-district-name.jpg`
+
+The 22-label inventory and widths are checked in full; not every guide/host was visited manually. Original Kanto story/recap, most original party/Bag/Pokédex/options details, Pokémon and move names, and most battle narration retain the documented English scope. This work does not claim full FireRed translation.
