+# Mapping handoff: Old Taichung Station arrival
+
+Status: handoff notes only. The user reassigned all compressed-city geometry, layouts, connections, warps, and spawn work to LANDMARKS / `feature/city-map` in `.worktrees/game-mapping`. This workstream stopped before making any Station source changes. No Station map, layout, connection, warp, spawn, or regional-section implementation exists in this branch.
+
+This document is a WIP proposal for the mapper to read, not an implementation commit to integrate as a playable Station release. The existing native working baseline remains unchanged.
+
+## Accepted design and source of truth
+
+The selected start is **Old Taichung Station plaza**, with a brief language choice, Taichung welcome, four actual starter choices, immediate cycling, and free exploration. Greenway remains a working district and its tea errand stays optional. There is no alternate-start selection feature.
+
+The parent project's `docs/game-design.md`, `landmark-shortlist.md`, `starting-location.md`, and `world-map-plan.md` hold the latest accepted scope and the proposed compressed-world structure. The ten retained landmarks are included; exact city geometry, leader characters, rosters, progression, and gym battle implementation remain separate work. No custom gyms are implemented in this handoff.
+
+## Agreed identifier coordination
+
+The browser/guide owner confirmed stable landmark ID **`old-taichung-station`**. Proposed native identifiers communicated to that owner are:
+
+- `MAP_TAICHUNG_OLD_STATION`, map folder/name `TaichungOldStation`.
+- `LAYOUT_TAICHUNG_OLD_STATION`, layout name `TaichungOldStation_Layout`.
+- Optional separate visitor hall: `MAP_TAICHUNG_OLD_STATION_VISITOR_HALL` and matching layout.
+- A distinct map-name section such as `MAPSEC_TAICHUNG_OLD_STATION`, with a short English banner until the localization owner covers that renderer.
+
+These map identifiers are a coordination proposal, not registered constants in this branch. The guide keeps Station planned/non-playable until the mapper and parent verify an integrated ROM. Greenway remains `calligraphy-greenway` / `MAP_PALLET_TOWN`.
+
+Final spawn, building footprint, door anchors, return warps, safe drop-off coordinates, and map dimensions belong to the mapper. My earlier 32×28 plaza with `(16,8)` spawn and a west street at rows 18–20 was only an unimplemented bounded prototype idea. It is not an accepted pixel layout and should not constrain the newer whole-city mapping brief.
+
+## Shared opening API: reuse it instead of copying gifts
+
+Current `data/maps/PalletTown/scripts.inc` exports the reusable script labels:
+
+- `Taichung_OnFrame`: an on-frame table that runs language selection when `VAR_0x40FB == 0`, then the existing welcome/starter flow when `VAR_0x40FC == 0`.
+- `Taichung_MigrateLegacyStarter`: safe transition/resume migration for older fixed-Bulbasaur prototype saves.
+- `Taichung_EventScript_ChooseLanguage`: the native menu's later language-switch entry.
+
+A new Station map can reference the same `Taichung_OnFrame` table from its own map-script header. Keep the opening/gift code in one place: four menu paths share one actual `givemon`, then seed supplies and the Bicycle once. Do not copy the starter grant or create a separate Station starter variable.
+
+The existing `Taichung_OnTransition` additionally marks Greenway visited and sets the Pallet heal location. Reusing that label wholesale at Station would mark Greenway visited before arrival. The mapper should decide on a Station transition/resume wrapper that invokes the shared migration without inventing another starter flow, and preserves a valid healing/respawn destination.
+
+Current persistent state:
+
+| Variable | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `VAR_0x40FB` | 0 unset, 1 English, 2 Traditional Chinese |
+| `VAR_0x40FC` | 0 unselected, otherwise the actual chosen starter species ID |
+| `VAR_0x40FD` | 0 uninitialized, 1 optional tea errand available, 2 carrying tea, 3 delivered |
+
+Continue must retain the chosen starter, language, position, and quest state. Migration must run on map resume as well as transition: the normal Continue path can call `ResumeMap` without an on-transition script. Existing Greenway saves should not be reset or relocated as an accidental side effect of changing only the new-game spawn.
+
+`src/new_game.c` currently uses `WarpToPlayersRoom()` to set the actual outdoor spawn to `MAP_PALLET_TOWN`, `(10,9)`. That legacy function name does not imply an indoor room. Ownership of this spawn change now belongs to the mapper.
+
+## Existing Greenway compatibility contract
+
+The current map is 24×28. Its north edge connects to `MAP_ROUTE1` at offset 0 and the original south-ocean connection is removed. All three existing exterior doors and interior return warps are valid:
+
+| Door | Exterior coordinate | Destination | Destination warp |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Guest house | `(6,7)` | `MAP_PALLET_TOWN_PLAYERS_HOUSE_1F` | 1 |
+| Tea house | `(15,7)` | `MAP_PALLET_TOWN_RIVALS_HOUSE` | 0 |
+| Field station | `(16,13)` | `MAP_PALLET_TOWN_PROFESSOR_OAKS_LAB` | 0 |
+
+Guide: `LOCALID_PALLET_SIGN_LADY` at `(6,22)`, elevation 3. Vendor: `LOCALID_PALLET_FAT_MAN` at `(16,8)`, elevation 3. Keep the vendor off `(15,8)`, which is the shop's door-approach cell. The latter local ID also has a linked-object reference in `Route21_North`.
+
+A future side connection needs reciprocal directions and matching offsets. Open traversable cells on both edges, not just JSON connection records. Keep closed tree art in full two-row pairs where possible, and verify that cycling across the seam reaches valid collision/elevation on the other map. The final placement belongs to the mapper.
+
+The current starter setup enables Pokémon/Pokédex menus, running, and saving; advances the old Oak/lab scenes; hides the lab's starter balls/rival; and enables guest-house healing. Those compatibility flags and the valid respawn should survive the map migration. See `docs/taichung-world-status.md` for the complete baseline contract.
+
+## Registration and regional-map safety findings
+
+Source inspection found 43 existing map groups, 383 layouts, and 197 regional sections at checkpoint `1c8d243`. Append new map-group/layout entries rather than inserting before existing entries, so current map/layout IDs remain stable. A new `gMapGroup_Taichung` appended to `group_order` was considered; no group has been created here.
+
+Map headers/events/connections and the constants headers are generated from `data/maps/map_groups.json`, each `map.json`, and `data/layouts/layouts.json`. Register new script/text includes in `data/event_scripts.s`. Do not hand-edit generated `.inc` or constants files.
+
+**Safety issue to resolve before appending a new map section:** `src/region_map.c::InitRegionMapType()` assumes every region section at or after `SEVII_MAPSEC_START` is present in `sSeviiMapsecs`. Its search loops until a match without a bound on the region-array index. A new appended Station section would not be in those island arrays. Merely keeping its number below 256 is insufficient; opening the native region map could read beyond the arrays.
+
+A small explicit Taichung/Kanto exception or a bounded/default-safe region lookup is needed if the mapper appends a Station map section. `GetMapName()` itself can use the generated appended name table, but that does not make the separate region-selection lookup safe. Also note that appending before the generated `MAPSEC_NONE` moves the sentinel's numeric value; preserve save compatibility deliberately.
+
+Native map banners currently use the legacy English renderer. The localization owner recommended a short English banner plus properly translated signs/NPC text until banner coverage is implemented.
+
+## Translation and art handoff
+
+The localization owner has queued changing the shared Chinese welcome from a Greenway-specific sentence to generic Taichung wording. The shared English welcome is already generic. Coordinate exact new Station text symbols with that owner rather than editing `charmap.txt`, rendering code, or the translation corpus independently.
+
+New native English Station signs/NPC text and any visitor-hall labels need a symbol/text list for the localization slice. No such text was authored here. Reused tiles and provisional building artwork are acceptable for the playable skeleton; a placeholder sign or façade must not imply completed bespoke station/clock-tower art or a working landmark gym.
+
+## Verification available and next checks
+
+The isolated `feature/world-gyms` bootstrap/build already reproduced ROM SHA-1 `8d0b2a311d40e14cfff035df28f9506e4801f569` without changing the canonical web ROM. The baseline map validator passed 378 reachable tiles, both NPCs, all signs, all three building approaches/return destinations, and the north route.
+
+The current root map validator requires a Pallet Town new-game spawn and the renderer selects the Pallet layout. The parent was asked to make them accept the new Station spawn/map while retaining Greenway's local door/NPC checks. Do not edit root helpers from the mapping worktree; coordinate the requested interface with the parent.
+
+Before integrating a Station release, verify the real new-game spawn, shared language/four-starter sequence, one-time gifts, route to Greenway and back, every door/return exit, indoor bike rejection, save/Continue, and a valid healing/respawn path. Existing Chinese/menu/bike browser proof for `8d0b2a31` is a baseline, not verification of a future Station build.
