+# Provisional Old City habitat
+
+The first city encounter table is deliberately small and provisional: **Pidgey 50% / Rattata 50%, levels 2–4**, native encounter rate **12**. Small birds and rodents suit the park lawns and the Station's urban garden. These are gameplay test defaults, not an approved final regional roster or balance target.
+
+The source table is in `src/data/wild_encounters.json`, native map `MAP_TAICHUNG_OLD_CITY`, base label `sTaichungOldCity`. It supplies land encounters only. The native engine uses one land table for the map, so the same small urban team appears on each authored Old City tall-grass patch:
+
+| Existing habitat | Local rectangle (inclusive) | Grass cells |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Park lawn west (`park-lawns`) | x20–21, y12–22 | 22 |
+| Park lawn east (`park-lawns-east`) | x35–36, y14–22 | 18 |
+| Station urban garden (`station-urban-garden`) | x17–23, y58–64 | 49 |
+
+The east park lawn is already authored in `tools/taichung/build_city.py` and the compiled layout. It was omitted from the mapper's initial habitat metadata. Main approved recording this existing grass in gameplay documentation and validation without rewriting geometry or the mapping contract.
+
+The table activates **89 existing reachable grass cells**. Ordinary paving and ornamental lawn do not have the native land-encounter attribute. No grass tile, collision, door, warp, connection, actor, or spawn was changed. Every landmark approach remains reachable without entering this Old City encounter grass. This keeps random battles optional even when the saved Wild setting is Normal.
+
+The other two new districts currently have no wild table. No water, fishing, Rock Smash, or new static encounter was added. Native legacy tables remain unchanged. Saved Wild Off suppresses these automatic grass encounters; Low applies the quarter-rate policy; Normal uses rate 12 with native cooldown, cycling, abilities, Repel, and rate modifiers.
+
+Run `python3 tools/taichung_gameplay/validate-encounters.py` from the game checkout. It resolves real metatile encounter attributes, checks that actual accessible Old City land-encounter grass exactly matches the announced habitats, verifies walking reachability and a route to every landmark that avoids this grass, validates native slot weights/species/levels, and reports weighted species shares. It reads the mapper contract and does not regenerate or modify maps.
+
+Native field sampling and catching/battle balance still require emulator verification after the city and exploration settings are integrated. A host rate test and a valid table do not prove observed random-encounter frequency.
