+# Saved exploration preferences
+
+The two controls target automatic interruptions while exploring. They do not disable deliberate battles or alter an active battle.
+
+## Save and behavior contract
+
+| Preference | Saved variable | Off (1) | Low (2) | Normal (3) |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Random wild encounters | `VAR_0x40F8` | No automatic land/water/roamer encounter starts | Quarter of the native effective encounter threshold, minimum 1 if positive | Native configured behavior |
+| Trainer sight challenges | `VAR_0x40F9` | NPCs do not initiate challenges on sight | Native sight range capped to one adjacent tile | Native configured range |
+
+Both variables were unused except their upstream constant definitions. Zero/unset and invalid values read as Normal without writing the save or replaying the introduction. They are independent of language `0x40FB`, starter `0x40FC`, optional quest `0x40FD`, and ten-gym completion `0x40FA`.
+
+`src/taichung_exploration.c` contains the saved policy and pure rate/range helpers. `StandardWildEncounter` checks the saved wild setting together with the existing temporary disable flag. Scripts can still temporarily disable encounters; calling `DisableWildEncounters(FALSE)` cannot override saved Off. No preference is stored in that temporary flag. Preference and City Pass reads access the current saved variables directly: native `VarGet` can replay an older quest-log value into the save, which must not roll back these current preferences or stamps.
+
+For Low, `DoWildEncounterRateTest` scales the final automatic dice threshold after native cycling, rate-buff, flute, Cleanse Tag, ability, and maximum-rate handling. Consequently the native rate buff cannot eventually bypass Low's reduction. This is initial tuning, not final habitat balance. The existing cooldown and the area's configured encounter data remain in place. The same automatic path covers walking, cycling, and surfing when available.
+
+The rate helper is explicitly limited to automatic encounters. Rock Smash, fishing, Sweet Scent, static Pokémon, and scripted/gym battles remain deliberate interactions. Trainer Off stops before the native sight scan; Low reuses native direction and collision checks with a one-tile range. It uses no per-frame random reroll. Voluntary trainer interaction and `StartTrainerBattle` are unchanged. Changing either setting never cancels or rewards an ongoing battle.
+
+## Native screens
+
+Fresh games call `TaichungExploration_ScriptOpenStartup` after the selected starter has actually been granted and its brief confirmation closes. The startup screen has two preference rows and Continue. It initially selects Continue; one A accepts both Normal defaults and enters exploration. Up/Down selects a row; Left/Right or A on a setting cycles Off, Low, Normal. B accepts the current pair and returns. All three choices remain visible for both settings.
+
+The existing OPTION / 設定 Start-menu row opens the same Exploration screen later. No tenth menu row or new global multichoice ID is added. A fourth `GAME OPTIONS / 遊戲設定` action preserves the original native options screen (text speed, battle style, sound, etc.). Exiting that screen returns to Exploration. Closing Exploration returns to the native field menu.
+
+Edits apply together when leaving the Exploration screen or opening Game Options. They live in the normal save block and are persisted by native Save/Continue. The startup call is inside the successful one-time starter flow; continuing an older save with unset preferences simply uses Normal and does not rerun language, starter, or settings onboarding.
+
+The native panel uses the existing Chinese renderer and a heap-backed window. Its only additional static EWRAM is eight bytes for callback and selection state. Labels and help text are English and Traditional Chinese; glyph generation scans `src/taichung*.c`.
+
+## Verification
+
+`bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-exploration.sh` compiles the actual policy and gym-progress modules with host saved-variable mocks. It tests all nine independent preference combinations, old/invalid defaults without writes, rate zero/minimum/quarter/large values, all configured sight ranges 0–255, deterministic repeated sight checks, temporary-disable/reset independence, and valid voluntary/active gym wins with both automatic controls Off. Only the reserved three preference/progress variables may be written in this fixture.
+
+`bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-progress.sh` separately retains the ten-gym win/loss/retry/duplicate guards. Forced outcomes exist only in host tests; the ROM has no automatic completion command.
+
+The first isolated build passes with 334 Chinese glyphs and EWRAM 261,060 bytes (8 bytes beyond the preceding City Pass build). After merging the native city, bridge, checkpoint/migration, and Old City encounter table, the combined build uses EWRAM 261,096 bytes (1,048 bytes remain). Integration must still regenerate the glyph union with the city translation slice. Native screen layout, preference Save/Continue, and representative field interruption checks must be proven in the browser after compilation; host mocks are not a native save-file proof.
