+# Ten landmark gym progress
+
+This module is a foundation for ten landmark gyms. It supplies saved completion state, a native City Pass, and one optional battle adapter. It does not add the final ten leader teams, rewards, balancing, or geometry. Those decisions remain open.
+
+## Stable save contract
+
+`VAR_0x40FA` stores the ten-bit completion mask (`0x0000`–`0x03FF`). It was unused in the pinned upstream and the existing prototype. The normal eight Kanto badge flags remain separate. Language (`0x40FB`), chosen starter (`0x40FC`), and optional tea errand (`0x40FD`) keep their existing meanings.
+
+| Bit / native ID | Stable guide ID | City Pass name |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 0 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_OLD_STATION` | `old-taichung-station` | Old Station / 舊臺中車站 |
+| 1 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_PARK` | `taichung-park` | Taichung Park / 臺中公園 |
+| 2 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_MIYAHARA` | `miyahara` | Miyahara / 宮原眼科 |
+| 3 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_SCIENCE_MUSEUM` | `natural-science-museum` | Science Museum / 科博館 |
+| 4 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_GREENWAY` | `calligraphy-greenway` | Greenway / 草悟道 |
+| 5 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_SHEN_JI` | `shen-ji-new-village` | Shen Ji Village / 審計新村 |
+| 6 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_FINE_ARTS` | `fine-arts-museum` | Fine Arts Museum / 美術館 |
+| 7 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_FENGJIA` | `fengjia-night-market` | Fengjia Market / 逢甲夜市 |
+| 8 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_MAPLE_GARDEN` | `maple-garden` | Maple Garden / 秋紅谷 |
+| 9 / `TAICHUNG_GYM_THEATER` | `taichung-theater` | Taichung Theater / 歌劇院 |
+
+Do not reorder these bits when changing the world map or display names. IDs outside 0–9 are rejected. Read APIs ignore the six unused high bits. Reads use the current save directly so a historical quest-log variable cannot roll back the displayed mask. This variable uses the existing native save/Continue storage; volatile challenge state is not saved and cannot complete a challenge after reloading.
+
+## Completion rule and reusable API
+
+`include/taichung_gym_progress.h` is the native interface. A gym script first calls `TaichungGymPrepareChallenge(gymId, trainerId)`. Preparing, displaying a dialogue, declining a battle, or reading the pass writes no completion bit.
+
+The normal trainer engine calls `TaichungGymOnTrainerBattleStart` from `StartTrainerBattle`, and `TaichungGymOnTrainerBattleEnd` from its actual end callback. A bit is written only when the prepared ID is valid, the expected trainer starts and finishes, and the result is exactly `B_OUTCOME_WON`. Loss, draw, escape, stale result, missing start, or a different trainer clears the pending challenge without writing. A completed gym cannot be prepared again. A duplicate battle-end callback cannot award another stamp. `TaichungGymCancelChallenge` clears a prepared challenge without progress; the Station adapter uses it if native trainer flags skip the actual battle, then returns control safely.
+
+`callnative` wrappers in `src/taichung_gym_adapter.c` expose the same API to future map scripts: set `VAR_0x8004` to the permanent gym ID and `VAR_0x8005` to the real trainer ID, then call `TaichungGym_ScriptPrepareChallenge`. `TaichungGym_ScriptIsComplete`, `TaichungGym_ScriptGetCompletedCount`, `TaichungGym_ScriptGetResult`, and `TaichungGym_ScriptCancelChallenge` return or clear state without global multichoice-table changes. Results use `VAR_RESULT`.
+
+Native battle money and experience retain FireRed's normal win behavior. This module gives no separate item, badge, money, or repeat reward. Native loss/whiteout behavior remains in the engine; the world owner is responsible for the Station heal/respawn checkpoint.
+
+## Native City Pass
+
+The existing Player row becomes **PASS / 城市護照**. It opens a two-column native GBA screen with all ten names, each `OK` or `--`, and the count out of ten. It adds no tenth Start menu row. **A** opens the original Trainer Card; returning from that card reopens the pass. **B** or **Start** returns to the field menu. The pass only reads saved completion; opening or closing it cannot award progress. The native Save summary and Continue preview also show `GYMS / 道館` and the same `0/10`–`10/10` count. The generic badge-count utilities, badge flags, HM checks, and original Trainer Card still use their native eight-badge state.
+
+English and Traditional Chinese use the existing native language preference and font renderer. The subtitle makes the entries gym stamps rather than a claim that the vanilla eight-badge Trainer Card now represents ten gyms.
+
+## Station battle adapter for the map owner
+
+Exported script entry: `TaichungGym_EventScript_StationChallenge` in `data/scripts/taichung_gyms.inc`. The map owner can point `TaichungCity_Host_OldStation` at this entry once the geometry branch is frozen. This gameplay change deliberately does not edit a map, room host, door, warp, connection, or spawn.
+
+The adapter offers an optional yes/no challenge. Declining returns immediately to exploration. The first win records Station bit 0; later interactions acknowledge the existing stamp and do not battle or reward again. A loss follows the real engine's whiteout and permits a later retry. Dialogue and battle intro/defeat text follow the current native language.
+
+The fixture is explicitly provisional: fictional **JUN / 俊**, a generic Youngster portrait with the native Leader class, **Rattata level 5** and **Pidgey level 6**, default moves, no held items, no battle items, no EV/IV tuning. Trainer ID `TRAINER_TAICHUNG_STATION_JUN` is 743; `NUM_TRAINERS` becomes 744, below the existing 768 trainer-flag capacity. This is a small urban test team, not an approved final roster or balance target.
+
+The other nine landmarks have independent saved states and display entries, but no automatic completion and no invented battle teams. Future adapters must call the same preparation API with their permanent ID and their own real trainer.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run `bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-progress.sh` from this game checkout. It compiles the real state module with host save-variable mocks and checks all ten distinct bits, stable order/IDs, count, every non-win outcome 0–15, missing/mismatched starts and ends, loss retry, cancellation, duplicates, invalid gym/trainer IDs, and that the only variable written is `0x40FA`. Forced outcomes exist only in this host test; no debug completion command ships in the ROM.
+
+The isolated source build uses the root project's `scripts/build-game.sh` with `TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE` set to this worktree. Generated Chinese glyph/charmap/menu changes are kept separate from gameplay source; integration must regenerate the union of native map, menu, and dialogue text.
+
+Actual Station battle/whiteout/Continue acceptance requires the map owner's adapter hook and the parent's Station respawn wiring. Compiling the optional unhooked script and host-testing the win guard do not by themselves prove that integrated gameplay path.
