@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# Native/browser language bridge, version 1
+
+The ROM exposes one 32-byte volatile EWRAM packet named `gTaichungLanguageBridge`. The browser may request a change to the saved language variable `0x40FB`; it does not edit party, location, quest, starter or gym state. The language remains part of the ordinary cartridge save, so the player uses the native Save action to retain it across a fresh cartridge boot.
+
+The packet is initialized at runtime and refreshed once per main-loop iteration after game callbacks. It is not a save format, ROM patch API, or fixed offset into the emulator's WebAssembly heap. The exact GBA symbol address is supplied by the matching ROM's `build.json` metadata. Version 1 in this isolated build is at `0x0203F468`; other source combinations must obtain the address from their own ELF/metadata.
+
+## Packet layout
+
+All multibyte fields are little endian and naturally aligned.
+
+| Byte offset | Type | Field | Value / ownership |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 0 | u32 | magicA | `0x414C4354` |
+| 4 | u32 | magicB | `0x3130474E`; together the words spell `TCLANG01` |
+| 8 | u16 | version | `1` |
+| 10 | u16 | size | `32` |
+| 12 | u32 | selfGbaAddress | Actual address of this EWRAM packet |
+| 16 | u32 | frameCounter | Advances every native loop; skips zero on wrap |
+| 20 | u8 | activeLanguage | ROM-owned: `0` unset/not ready, `1` English, `2` Traditional Chinese |
+| 21 | u8 | requestedLanguage | Browser-owned request value, only `1` or `2` |
+| 22 | u8 | flags | Bit 0: save variables ready. Bit 1: safe overworld state |
+| 23 | u8 | result | Result of the last acknowledged sequence, below |
+| 24 | u32 | requestSequence | Browser-owned, nonzero sequence number |
+| 28 | u32 | ackSequence | ROM-owned; written after applying or rejecting that request |
+
+Result codes are `0` none, `1` applied, `2` superseded by an explicit native choice, `3` rejected before a native language was chosen, and `4` invalid request value. The result remains available until another request is acknowledged. The ROM clears `requestedLanguage` when acknowledging.
+
+## Browser contract
+
+The browser first verifies the fetched ROM digest against its build metadata. It then discovers the packet in the pinned emulator's current `HEAPU8`, requiring both magic words, version, size, the exact metadata address in `selfGbaAddress`, and a changing frame counter. A ROM byte buffer or frozen save-state copy is not a valid live packet. More than one advancing candidate must fail discovery rather than guessing. A paused runtime cannot complete this liveness probe until it resumes. Rediscover after a new runtime, heap replacement, restart or imported state.
+
+Only bytes 21 and 24–27 are writable by the client. Publish `requestedLanguage` first, then publish a new nonzero `requestSequence` last, using aligned atomic stores for shared heap access. Keep at most one outstanding sequence. Read the acknowledgement/result together with a stable packet snapshot. Do not treat a request as applied until its sequence is acknowledged with result 1. Result 2 means the browser adopts the native choice. Do not reuse a sequence or overwrite an outstanding request; increment with unsigned wrap and skip zero.
+
+An initial browser preference never answers the ROM's startup menu: `activeLanguage == 0` is authoritative. Once native language is known, native menu changes publish back to the browser, and deliberate subsequent browser choices can send requests. A pending request while the emulator is paused or the game is busy remains pending until a safe native frame. Invalid/pre-choice requests are acknowledged without changing the saved variable.
+
+## Native guards and conflict handling
+
+The save pointer must be aligned and contained in EWRAM, and the normal overworld callback must have been entered before the bridge reads the language variable. Publication reads the raw variable directly to avoid `VarGet`'s quest-log replay side effects.
+
+Applying a browser request additionally requires both exact normal field callbacks, a frame in which ordinary game callbacks ran, no battle, palette fade, link state, locked player controls, active script, visible field message, active text printer or quest-log playback. A main-loop tick during Help or the save-failure overlay cannot apply a request. The only write is the original `VarSet(0x40FB, language)` call at that safe point.
+
+Both C `VarSet` and the script engine's direct `setvar` path notify the bridge only for `0x40FB`. A native menu selection immediately acknowledges an older pending browser request as result 2, including selecting the language already in use. The bridge suppresses that notification around its own write. Other variables retain their original setter behavior. A raw native language change outside those paths is also detected on the following tick.
+
+The generated font/localization module remains separate from the bridge. Running the canonical Chinese generator does not rewrite these protocol or engine adapter files.
+
+## Checks
+
+The host check compiles the actual protocol source, then covers packet layout/signature, startup protection, 60 busy frames followed by application, writer-before-ack ordering, duplicate sequence suppression, explicit native re-selection, raw native change, invalid values, failed writes, zero sequences, frame wrap, stale packet reinitialization and unrelated save-state sentinels.
+
+```sh
+cc -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Iinclude \
+  tests/test_taichung_language_bridge.c src/taichung_language_bridge_protocol.c \
+  -o /tmp/test-taichung-language-bridge
+/tmp/test-taichung-language-bridge
+```
+
+The native ROM compiles at 16,777,216 bytes. EWRAM usage is 261,076 of 262,144 bytes, leaving 1,068 bytes; IWRAM usage is 29,824 of 32,768. The bridge build before its source commit has SHA-1 `550080af3d845ff50ce02a6163e20c36905ea894` and SHA-256 `6d7e3c1111c3cf6b8510f2111e9340a59d05889fea60bafcfc38a6f4b8fddcd9`.
+
+## Live emulator proof
+
+Verified this exact ROM on the isolated `127.0.0.1:5175` fixture, without editing the integration checkout. The fixture used a copied web build, SRAM-only cartridge boot, and a test-only getter for the pinned runtime's private `HEAPU8`. A diagnostic panel made requests by writing only the two client-owned packet fields. This establishes native protocol behavior; the production browser selector/getter integration is a separate task.
+
+1. The ROM's SHA-256 matched its metadata. Scanning the current heap found exactly one matching-address packet, at heap offset `0xB3468`. Its frame counter changed on all three 250 ms liveness samples; its self address matched ELF/metadata `0x0203F468`.
+2. On New Game, the visible native English/Chinese choice had active language 0. A Chinese request, sequence 1, was acknowledged with result 3 and left that choice unanswered. English was then selected natively, and one Charmander was chosen.
+3. While the native Start menu remained open, Chinese request 2 stayed pending for 6.4 seconds: active 1, requested 2, flags 1, acknowledgement still 1. Closing the menu caused result 1, active 2, flags 3 and acknowledgement 2. Reopening Start visibly rendered the Chinese labels.
+4. English request 3 stayed pending while the player opened the native Language menu. Explicitly choosing the already-active Chinese option acknowledged it with result 2 and retained active 2. This proves the same-value native-selection hook rather than merely detecting a changed variable.
+5. Invalid language 9 was acknowledged with result 4 and left Chinese active. A subsequent native English choice published active 1 without inventing a new acknowledgement. Safe-field Chinese, English and Chinese requests 5, 6 and 7 each received result 1.
+6. A request made from the party screen remained pending through returning to the still-open Start menu. Only closing Start applied it. The final Chinese request 9 was acknowledged successfully in the free field.
+7. The party contained exactly one level-five Charmander with 20/20 HP in this new game. The player remained on the same plaza tile throughout these changes; language and starter selection did not restart.
+
+Evidence is stored in the parent project's ignored `artifacts/worktrees/8d9e3f9b98e8/` namespace:
+
