+- `qa-native-chinese-save-complete.jpg`
+- `qa-saved-position.jpg`
+- `qa-unsaved-movement.jpg`
+- `qa-cartridge-continue-menu.jpg`
+- `qa-position-after-continue.jpg`
+- `qa-chinese-menu-after-continue.jpg`
+- `qa-party-after-continue.jpg`
+
+The earlier checkpoint also passed Chinese introduction/starter/Start-menu rendering, Bike/Get off, indoor cycling rejection and changing language without losing party or position. The four starter branches were unchanged by canonical regeneration and were not redundantly retested here.
+
+## Native language bridge
+
+The bridge is a separate module from the generated font/translation source. It publishes the native language in a 32-byte versioned EWRAM packet and accepts only English/Chinese requests at a safe normal field frame. The initial native choice remains authoritative. A newer explicit native choice cancels an older queued browser request, including reselecting the current language.
+
+The host protocol check and actual emulator checks pass: unique advancing heap discovery against exact ROM metadata, startup rejection, queued requests through native Start/party menus, both language values applying after return to the field, native-choice precedence, invalid-value rejection, and intact starter party/location. The tested bridge ROM has SHA-1 `550080af3d845ff50ce02a6163e20c36905ea894`, SHA-256 `6d7e3c1111c3cf6b8510f2111e9340a59d05889fea60bafcfc38a6f4b8fddcd9`. See the bridge document for the packet contract, source-specific memory budget, exact runtime evidence and remaining production-browser checks.
