+# City save and Station checkpoint
+
+Save version 1 uses reserved variable `0x40F7`. Existing allocations remain
+`40F8` wild preference, `40F9` trainer-sight preference, `40FA` ten-gym mask,
+`40FB` language, `40FC` chosen starter species and `40FD` tea quest.
+
+New games start at Old City `(30,66)` and use that outdoor Station checkpoint.
+The native whiteout routine still applies its normal money loss and heals the
+party. A city checkpoint then returns directly through the normal field fade,
+without running a Pokemon Center nurse script against an outdoor NPC.
+
+On native Continue, unversioned Taichung saves with a party and a recognized
+starter marker are upgraded once. The earliest fixed-Bulbasaur prototype is
+recognized by its nonzero tea marker. Saves in the thirteen city maps retain
+their map/position; older prototype areas use the engine's Continue warp to
+arrive at the Station. The party, bag, city stamps, tea state and preferences
+are retained. An unset legacy language becomes English; Chinese remains
+Chinese. An untouched vanilla FireRed save has neither prototype marker and
+is not migrated. A new game retains the mandatory native language choice.
+
+ROM-specific browser snapshots deliberately use different namespaces. To move
+progress between ROM revisions, export/import the native `.sav`, then choose
+native Continue. The new version is persisted on the next native Save.
+
+Runtime validation of the combined release is recorded by the integrator.
