+# Taichung world and native-menu status
+
+This document records the playable foundation at game checkpoint `1c8d243002fb4d36f2ef28e217e46f17235dff80` and the isolated `feature/world-gyms` worktree verification on 7 November 2026. No new world areas or custom gyms are added by this status commit.
+
+The intended final world is a compressed Taichung with recognizable landmarks, fictional gym leaders, and environment-appropriate encounters. The existing Greenway neighborhood is the first area of that larger world. Final landmarks, topology, gym count/order, leaders, badges, rosters, habitats, and species tables remain design decisions. A named sign, reused building, or browser guide marker does not mean a custom gym battle exists.
+
+## Ownership and integration boundaries
+
+- `feature/world-gyms` owns this world/status work and retains native menu ownership in `src/start_menu.c`. Future map layout, collision, door, object-event, and world-route edits should be scoped here after landmark decisions are approved.
+- The localization workstream owns font/glyph generation, encoding, rendering, `charmap.txt`, `src/taichung_language.c`, `include/taichung_language.h`, and translated text. Coordinate changes to shared Pallet Town script/text files, startup state, and menu language interfaces with that workstream before editing.
+- The browser/guide workstream owns the companion landmark catalog, web controls, guide, and browser/ROM language bridge. Coordinate stable landmark IDs and explicit game-area references with it.
+- The parent integration task owns the canonical `vendor/pokefirered` checkout, root project helpers/docs, canonical web ROM, and source integration. Development worktrees must not write those source files or replace the canonical web ROM.
+- Changes to `src/start_menu.c` must retain the native save/Continue path, field task cleanup, bike eligibility, and language-change script contract. No bicycle-engine modifications were needed for the current menu action.
+
+## Current map identity and topology
+
+| Property | Current value |
+| --- | --- |
+| Internal map ID | `MAP_PALLET_TOWN` |
+| Internal map name/layout | `PalletTown` / `LAYOUT_PALLET_TOWN` |
+| Region section | `MAPSEC_PALLET_TOWN`, labeled `TAICHUNG GREENWAY` |
+| Size | 24 columns × 28 rows; each metatile is 16×16 pixels |
+| New-game spawn | `(10, 9)` |
+| Weather and movement | Sunny; running and cycling allowed outdoors |
+| North connection | `MAP_ROUTE1`, direction up, offset 0 |
+| North exit cells | `(12, 0)` and `(13, 0)` |
+| South boundary | Solid trees on rows 26–27; old Route 21 south connection removed |
+| Respawn | `HEAL_LOCATION_PALLET_TOWN` |
+
+Keep the original internal map ID until a deliberate migration updates every reference. It is also the companion guide's current `gameAreaRef` for the playable Greenway area. The original Route 1 encounter table remains in use; a final Taichung habitat roster is not implemented.
+
+## Door and NPC contract
+
+Coordinates are zero-based metatile coordinates. All three exterior doors keep their original footprint and interior destination.
+
+| Exterior door | Coordinate | Destination | Destination warp index |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Guest house | `(6, 7)` | `MAP_PALLET_TOWN_PLAYERS_HOUSE_1F` | 1 |
+| Tea house | `(15, 7)` | `MAP_PALLET_TOWN_RIVALS_HOUSE` | 0 |
+| Field station | `(16, 13)` | `MAP_PALLET_TOWN_PROFESSOR_OAKS_LAB` | 0 |
+
+The player approaches these north-facing doors from the cell immediately south. Preserve the interior return warps and their destination IDs if the exterior changes. The guest-house host can heal the party. Existing interior artwork and most legacy Kanto content remain in place.
+
+| Actor | Local ID | Coordinate/elevation | Function |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Greenway guide | `LOCALID_PALLET_SIGN_LADY` | `(6, 22)`, elevation 3 | Optional tea delivery completion and directions |
+| Tea vendor | `LOCALID_PALLET_FAT_MAN` | `(16, 8)`, elevation 3 | Optional tea errand; stands beside the shop entrance |
+| Legacy Oak object | `LOCALID_PALLET_PROF_OAK` | `(10, 8)`, elevation 3 | Hidden using the original hide flag |
+
+The two quest NPCs are stationary. The vendor must not move to `(15, 8)`: that cell is the tea-house door approach. `LOCALID_PALLET_FAT_MAN` also has a legacy linked-object reference in `Route21_North`; coordinate any local-ID removal or renaming. The indoor tea-house host shares the same optional errand state.
+
+The map has five reachable signs: guest house `(4, 7)`, tea house `(13, 7)`, town `(9, 11)`, Greenway `(5, 14)`, and field station `(16, 16)`. Original Oak cutscene coordinate triggers are removed.
+
+## Persistent state and early-game flags
+
+| State | Value/meaning | Ownership |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `VAR_0x40FB` | 0 unset, 1 English, 2 Traditional Chinese | Localization; do not reuse |
+| `VAR_0x40FC` | 0 unselected; otherwise actual chosen starter species ID | Starter/save contract; do not reuse |
+| `VAR_0x40FD` | 0 uninitialized, 1 optional errand available, 2 carrying tea, 3 delivered | Local optional quest; do not reuse |
+
+Native starter order is Charmander, Bulbasaur, Squirtle, Pikachu. The selected species is granted once at level 5, followed by five Poké Balls, three Potions, and a Bicycle. The legacy three-way `VAR_STARTER_MON` remains valid for original Kanto scripts: Bulbasaur 0, Squirtle 1, Charmander 2; Pikachu uses safe legacy index 0 while its real species is preserved in `VAR_0x40FC`.
+
+First-frame initialization follows the original map-flag reset. The dedicated starter variable prevents repeated gifts on return/Continue. Earlier fixed-Bulbasaur prototype saves are migrated on both map transition and resume without changing their party. Language selection precedes the intro/starter choice and later changes preserve the adventure. The tea errand never gates movement or encounters.
+
+The initial setup enables `FLAG_SYS_POKEMON_GET`, `FLAG_SYS_POKEDEX_GET`, `FLAG_SYS_B_DASH`, and `FLAG_OPENED_START_MENU`. It sets `FLAG_BEAT_RIVAL_IN_OAKS_LAB` for guest-house healing, hides the three lab starter balls and rival, clears `FLAG_HIDE_OAK_IN_HIS_LAB`, and advances the old Oak/lab scene variables to 1/6. Preserve these compatibility choices until replacements cover the affected original story paths.
+
+## Native menu and cycling
+
+Normal field menu order is Pokédex, Pokémon, Bag, Bike/Get off, Player, Save, Language, Option, Exit. All nine rows fit the GBA display. The original HELP footer is suppressed for menus longer than seven rows so it cannot cover the last two actions; shorter specialized menus retain it.
+
+The Bike action invokes the existing `FieldUseFunc_Bike` task in registered-item field context. FireRed retains its indoor, water, rail, and forced-cycling eligibility checks, movement, animation, and task cleanup. Its label changes to `GET OFF` / `下車` while riding. The action is available immediately; no purchase, voucher, or unlock quest is required. YouBike rental stations and ride-hailing remain future work.
+
+Language closes the field menu and starts `Taichung_EventScript_ChooseLanguage`. Menu labels use the localization API `TaichungText(english, chinese)`. Preserve that API and script label, or coordinate both sides of any replacement.
+
+## Landmark and future gym coordination
+
+The existing companion catalog contains these stable IDs. They are coordination identifiers, not a final gym roster:
+
+| Landmark ID | Current game-area reference | Current implementation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `calligraphy-greenway` | `MAP_PALLET_TOWN` | Playable prototype neighborhood; no custom gym |
+| `cmp-park-lane` | None | Guide/planning entry only |
+| `fine-arts-museum` | None | Guide/planning entry only |
+| `natural-science-museum` | None | Guide/planning entry only |
+| `taichung-theater` | None | Guide/planning entry only |
+
+Before implementing a landmark gym, agree on its stable landmark ID, game map/layout ID, entrance and return-warp coordinates, safe transport drop-off coordinates/elevation/facing, fictional leader ID, battle/roster ID, badge/completion flag, and bilingual display text. Allocate new native flags/variables centrally so they cannot collide with the three persistent variables above. Numeric battle order and badge index should remain separate from stable landmark identity.
+
+Do not mark a guide entry playable or expose a fast-travel destination until its actual map, collision, warps, and safe landing cell exist. Final leader names, personalities, species, levels, and encounter triggers are still undecided. No new areas, gym IDs, trainer rosters, or encounter tables are created in this worktree checkpoint.
+
+## Isolated build verification
+
+Verification used the existing project helpers with `TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE` set to this worktree. Compiler objects and generated game files remain inside the worktree; exported ROM, log, and source-map rendering use the separate path namespace `3c6cc7b4e276`.
+
+```sh
+TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE=/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/.worktrees/game-world \
+  bash /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/scripts/bootstrap-game.sh
+TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE=/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/.worktrees/game-world \
+  bash /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/scripts/build-game.sh
+TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE=/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/.worktrees/game-world \
+  python3 /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/scripts/validate-game-map.py
+TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE=/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/.worktrees/game-world \
+  /Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 \
+  /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/scripts/render-game-map.py
+```
+
+Bootstrap succeeded with the existing pinned agbcc compiler and ARM binutils. The isolated shell selected Apple's Python without Pillow, so rendering used the already-installed Python 3.11 interpreter containing Pillow; no helper or system-package change was required.
+
+The independent build reproduced the checkpoint ROM byte for byte:
+
+- SHA-1: `8d0b2a311d40e14cfff035df28f9506e4801f569`.
+- SHA-256: `94d318ef2d25c474d02f0d5fb6d51b94f65c1f4d34e7d65b10411da53aa09317`.
+- Size: 16,777,216 bytes.
+- Isolated output: `/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/3c6cc7b4e276/roms/taichung-firered.gba`.
+- Build metadata/log: the same namespace's `roms/build.json` and `game-build.log`.
+- Rendered source map: the same namespace's `taichung-map.png`.
+
+The canonical web ROM retained the same SHA-1 before and after this isolated build. The integration source checkout stayed clean at `1c8d243` during verification.
+
+Map validation passes with 378 reachable tiles from `(10, 9)`. Both quest NPC interaction spaces, all five signs, all three door approaches and interior-return destinations, and the north Route 1 exit are valid. The closed south tree wall has no walkable hole. No native source fix was necessary.
+
+The same compiled `8d0b2a31` ROM had already passed actual browser QA for Chinese startup/dialogue/menu rendering, one real starter, cycling and dismounting, indoor cycling rejection, restored movement, and language switching with the party/location preserved. That UI pass was not repeated for this byte-identical isolated build. Browser/ROM language synchronization and untranslated legacy gameplay text remain separate localization/integration work.
